    "suspected_causes": [
      "All 4 ISP international gateways unreachable from external probes (TIC 2.187.1.1: connection refused, TIC 78.38.112.1: timeout, Irancell 5.232.0.1: timeout, Asiatech 94.182.0.1: timeout) while foreign-platform HTTP probes reach Google/YouTube/GitHub in 59-165ms — centralized DPI whitelisting at national gateway layer consistent with Bock et al. FOCI'20 whitelister architecture",
      "Irancell gateway error shifted from 'connection refused' to 'i/o timeout' compared to prior pass — may indicate DPI rule-state fluctuation at TIC gateway handling Irancell traffic, where connection refused reflects active TCP RST injection vs. timeout reflecting silent packet drop",
      "Protocol whitelist enforcement stable at 4.2% — 45 of 1,068 labeled IP ranges reachable across 78 operators, unchanged from prior pass; UDP/ICMP/SSH/VPN silently dropped at gateway — institutionalized whitelist architecture per IRBlock (Tai et al.) USENIX Security '25",
      "Electro DNS (78.157.42.100) persistently timing out while Shecan (178.22.122.100, 227ms) and TIC DNS (217.218.155.155, 225ms) remain fast — sustained targeted suppression of anti-censorship DNS resolver infrastructure, consistent with mandatory national DNS routing enforcement",
      "Asiatech dual failure persists — gateway (94.182.0.1 timeout) + web portal (www.asiatech.ir deadline exceeded) both down across all observed passes — ISP-specific isolation, likely CRA directive targeting or sustained infrastructure degradation",
      "Snapp (snapp.ir) remains in redirect-loop error state (stopped after 10 redirects) — consistent with prior pass; cycling between redirect loop and TLS handshake failure across sessions indicates DPI rule-state fluctuation across multiple DPI nodes rather than deliberate policy change",
      "Shaparak payment gateway (www.shaparak.ir) deadline-exceeded timeout persists — domestic payment infrastructure degradation or targeted application-layer filtering at gateway",
      "Snowflake broker latency continued normalizing to 497ms (from 614ms prior pass, 1,486ms two passes ago) — confirms prior spike was transient WebRTC relay congestion, not sustained anti-circumvention escalation",
      "Foreign platforms remain fast and stable (Google 59ms, YouTube 165ms, Wikipedia 105ms, GitHub 96ms, Cloudflare 182ms, Telegram 442ms, WhatsApp 93ms, Instagram 424ms) — economic-necessity whitelisting under selective-internet model fully maintained",
      "Circumvention tools externally reachable and healthy (Psiphon 133ms, Tor 495ms, BridgeDB 562ms, Snowflake 497ms) — all tools operational from external vantage; Snowflake continued latency normalization across three consecutive passes",
      "Saman Bank remains degraded at 3,002ms (borderline threshold) — elevated but functional, likely NIN congestion rather than filtering; no change from prior pass",
